    "result_text": "The full build succeeds. The implementation is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field derived from an owner's city using the fixed city-to-region table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Locality.java`** (new) \u2014 a helper class following the existing `MembershipTier`/`MembershipNumber` pattern. It holds the pinned `Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD` table and `of(city)` returns the canonical region, or `\"UNKNOWN\"` for any unlisted (or null) city.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that populates the DTO's `locality` from `Locality.of(owner.getCity())`, alongside the other derived fields.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and it appears in the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 NSW for Sydney, `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 UNKNOWN for a random city) pass, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nThe change fits the OfficeFloor architecture: `locality` is a purely derived, seed-independent field exposed through the mapper at the response edge \u2014 no new pipeline step was needed since it derives from state already on the loaded `Owner`.",
